{"name":"Terrazzo Brown","hex":"#a28873","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"terrazzo","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A faux-marble material used for flooring and countertops."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/terrazzo"},{"term":"brown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour like that of chocolate or coffee.","One of the colour balls used in snooker, with a value of 4 points."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a brown color/colour.","Gloomy."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brown"}],"entries":[{"title":"Terrazzo","blocks":[{"text":"Terrazzo is a composite material, poured in place or precast, which is used for floor and wall treatments. It consists of chips of marble, quartz, granite, glass, or other suitable material, poured with a cementitious binder, polymeric, or a combination of both. Metal strips often divide sections, or changes in color or material in a pattern. Additional chips may be sprinkled atop the mix before it sets. After it is cured it is ground and polished smooth or otherwise finished to produce a uniformly textured surface. \"Terrazzo\" is also often used to describe any pattern similar to the original terrazzo floors.\nModern forms of terrazzo include polished concrete."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Terrazzo_entryway.jpg/330px-Terrazzo_entryway.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrazzo"},{"title":"Brown","blocks":[{"text":"Brown is a color. It can be thought as a darker, typically desaturated shade of orange, and can often be produced by combining red and yellow with another color, namely blue."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg/330px-Espresso-roasted_coffee_beans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brown"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg/500px-Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg/500px-Hollywood_Walk_of_Fame_%287960322318%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the most well known examples of terrazzo flooring is the Hollywood Walk of Fame.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHollywood_Walk_of_Fame_(7960322318).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Pima1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Pima1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Terrazzo with stylized Native-American design at the Hoover Dam","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APima1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG/500px-Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG/500px-Gamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Terrazzo wall at the Gamla stan metro station, Stockholm","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGamla_stan_tunnelbana_terrazzo_070330.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Medved_mzoo.jpg/330px-Medved_mzoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Medved_mzoo.jpg/330px-Medved_mzoo.jpg?ut